## Original Content
The world largely moved on from the Rohingya crisis. But the exodus has not stopped, aid is shrinking and a generation of refugees is growing up with little prospect of going home.<br />

## Summary
Nine years after the Rohingya crisis began, it has entered a dangerous phase with ongoing exodus, reduced aid, and a refugee generation facing no hope of return. The international community has largely neglected this humanitarian disaster, exacerbating the situation.

## Key Points
- The world has largely moved on from the Rohingya crisis, leading to decreased attention and support.
- The exodus of Rohingya people continues, with no signs of stopping.
- Aid for Rohingya refugees is shrinking, impacting their well-being and future prospects.
- A generation of refugees is growing up with little to no prospect of returning to their homes.


